From: arr-optimized <arr-optimized@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] Optimize settings page: live, adjustable optimization
 settings

Adds Settings > Optimize (/settings/optimize) and GET/PUT /api/v3/config/optimize,
GET /api/v3/config/optimize/settings and /status.

Every tunable value of the series is an "optimize*" Config row through
IConfigService (additive), overridable by an ARR_* environment variable
(environment > saved > default; a valid variable locks the field and PUT
ignores it). Values apply on Save without a restart: one immutable
OptimizeSettings snapshot is swapped on ApplicationStartedEvent and
ConfigSavedEvent; hot paths read it with one volatile read.

- Indexer request spacing, cache hit header/value and grab spacing replace
  the read-once environment options (same variables, same stock defaults;
  a grab at 2000 ms is exactly the stock call).
- ffprobe timeout is a setting (default 15 min, 0 = stock calls with no
  timeout).
- Custom format cache and ffprobe cache limits and lifetimes are settings;
  changes trim or clear the caches under their existing locks; 0 = off runs
  the stock path. The decision-batch memo can be switched off (stock reads).
- Status: built-in optimizations and Interlocked counters since start-up.
- ffprobe cache settle time, unsettled lifetime and failure lifetime can only
  be made stricter than next3 (settle >= 60 s, unsettled <= 60 s, failure
  <= 10 min): the cache matches on the file stamp alone.
- PUT changes only the values present in the body; an explicit null resets.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
